      "text": "Let $\\angle ABE = n$.  Then $\\angle OBE = 90^\\circ - n$ and $\\angle BAE = 43^\\circ$.  Thus $\\angle EBO = 90^\\circ - n - 43^\\circ = 47^\\circ - n$.  Since $\\angle BCA = \\angle AEB = 90^\\circ$, $\\angle ABC = \\angle ABE = n$.  Then $\\angle ABC = \\angle ABE + \\angle EBC = n + \\angle EBC = n + \\angle BBE = n + 47^\\circ - n = 47^\\circ$, so $\\angle BAAE = \\angle EAE + \\angle AEE + \\angle BEC = \\angle EAE + 2\\angle BBE + 90^\\circ = \\angle EAE + 90^\\circ$.  Since $\\angle EAE = 180^\\circ - \\angle EBO$, $\\angle CED = 180^\\circ - \\angle EBO = 180^\\circ - (47^\\circ - n) + 180^\\circ - (360^\\circ - 2\\cdot360^\\circ + 43^\\circ) = 180^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n - 360^\\circ + 2\\cdot360^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n - 360^\\circ + 720^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n - 360^\\circ + 720^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 180^\\circ + 2\\cdot313^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n = 180^\\circ + 626^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n = 806^\\circ - 47^\\circ + n = 759^\\circ + n$.\n\nSince $43^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 78^\\circ = 43^\\circ + (n + 90^\\circ) = 43^\\circ + 133^\\circ = 176^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 4^\\circ = 360^\\circ - 176^\\circ$, $43^\\circ + n = 176^\\circ$, thus $n = 176^\\circ - 43^\\circ = 133^\\circ$.  Therefore, $n + 176^\\circ = \\boxed{313^\\circ}$. The answer is: 313",
